  "worked_solution": "Integrating the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now plot the solution curves by selecting different values for $C.$ The sketch below shows the solution curves for $C=-3,0,3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14041209/assets/2d64c09661973b7ef840e783a88de85d5ca9cf3436fae7eaebef36aca98ae631.png)",
